--- body ---
## Scope

Add the benchmark-supported configurations as curated registry rows and one
entry-id selector. This exposes candidates; it does not select a winner.

## Exit criteria

- Unset configuration still resolves to the incumbent MiniLM entry.
- Each row is complete and pinned; no raw per-field user overrides exist.
- Unknown or incomplete entries fail explicitly before index access.
- Index coexistence and invalidation use the complete entry fingerprint.

## Post-merge verification, 2026-09-03 (fork conductor-integration@d0a7660)

All four criteria hold.

- **Unset configuration resolves to the incumbent** — `selectEmbedderEntry()`
  with no id returns `INCUMBENT_LOCAL_ENTRY`, asserted after the alternatives
  are added.
- **Rows complete and pinned; no raw per-field overrides** — `revision` must be
  a 40-character commit SHA, `graphFile` must be the one `dtype` selects, and
  every vector field must carry a `sources` note. The only user-facing knob is
  `ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_MODEL`, which takes a curated entry id; a raw model
  repository is refused by design.
- **Unknown or incomplete entries fail explicitly before index access** — rows
  are parsed at module load, and `selectEmbedderEntry` throws on an unknown id
  naming the available ones.
- **Index coexistence and invalidation use the complete entry fingerprint** —
  the index key is `local:registry-v<fingerprint>` for every entry but the
  incumbent, which keeps its historic `local:<model>` key only while its live
  fingerprint computes equal to the frozen legacy digest.

One caveat inherited from 0490 and recorded there: a vector field added later
can be declared authoritative and still be absent from the fingerprint, which
would make two such entries share an index key.
